## `ab_steps_data` and `get_ab_steps`

`ab_steps_data` and `get_ab_steps` are the same method under two names. The
library's docs use `get_ab_steps`, the name of the analysis tools;
`ab_steps_data` exists so that every widget has a `<widget>_data` twin. The full
parameter and column reference is on the
[A/B Step Screen](/docs/tools/get-ab-steps) page.

### As a table for export

[`get_ab_steps_table`](/docs/tools/get-ab-steps-table) takes the same arguments
and returns the frame pivoted into the shape of the diff step matrix: one row
per event, and for every step a group of statistic columns (`values=`, by
default the delta, its interval and the adjusted p-value). Nothing is
recomputed. `to_csv` and `to_excel` write the two header rows, and
`styled=True` returns a pandas `Styler` with this widget's encoding, which
`to_excel` keeps:

```python
table = stream.get_ab_steps_table(diff, max_steps=8, assignment=assignment)
table.to_csv("steps.csv")             # pd.read_csv("steps.csv", header=[0, 1], index_col=0)
stream.get_ab_steps_table(diff, max_steps=8, styled=True).to_excel("steps.xlsx")
```

See also [A/B Transitions](/docs/widgets/ab-transitions), the same matrix per
edge.

